==English==
===Etymology===
From Latin '''[[quietus#Latin|quietus]]'''

===Pronunciation===
\kwy-EE-tus\

===Noun===
# a stillness or pause; something that quiets or represses; removal from activity; especially: death
# final settlement (as of a debt)

====Example====
"The constant rain and the cold have combined to put a quietus on outdoor activities." (Glenn Tucker, quoted in the Bangor Daily News [Maine], Oct. 10, 2005)

====Related Terms====
*[[quiescence]]
*[[quiet]]
*[[quietude]]

